sis.Complex.Polynomial.Basic\\n\\n/-!\\n# APM a92J05: Counting roots outside the unit disk via Rouché\\n\\n**Problem.** How many solutions does z¹⁰ + 5z³ + 2z + 1 = 0 have in the\\nregion {|z| > 1} (counted with multiplicity)?\\n\\n**Answer:** 7.\\n\\n## Proof strategy\\n\\nApply Rouché's theorem on |z| = 1. Write p(z) = g(z) + h(z) where\\ng(z) = 5z³ and h(z) = z¹⁰ + 2z + 1. On |z| = 1:\\n|h(z)| ≤ |z¹⁰| + |2z| + 1 = 4 < 5 = |g(z)|.\\nBy Rouché, p has the same number of zeros inside the disk as g = 5z³,\\nwhich has 3 (all at z = 0). Total = 10 (FTA), so outside = 10 − 3 = 7.\\n\\n## Statement repair note\\n\\nThe informal proof proposes using `∫` contour integrals for Rouché. Since\\nMathlib does not have Rouché's theorem, we state the result as a theorem\\nwith the Rouché step marked as a genuine sorry boundary, and prove all\\nthe supporting lemmas (degree, Rouché bound on circle, no roots on circle,\\nroot partition) zero-sorry.\\n-/\\n\\nset_option linter.unusedVariables false in\\nnoncomputable section\\n\\nopen Complex Polynomial Metric\\nopen scoped Polynomial\\n\\nnamespace ApmCanaries.A92J05\\n\\n/-- The polynomial p(z) = z¹⁰ + 5z³ + 2z + 1. -/\\ndef p : ℂ[X] := X ^ 10 + C (5 : ℂ) * X ^ 3 + C (2 : ℂ) * X + C (1 : ℂ)\\n\\n/-- The dominant term g(z) = 5z³. -/\\ndef g : ℂ[X] := C (5 : ℂ) * X ^ 3\\n\\n/-- The remainder h(z) = z¹⁰ + 2z + 1. -/\\ndef h : ℂ[X] := X ^ 10 + C (2 : ℂ) * X + C (1 : ℂ)\\n\\n/-- p = g + h. -/\\nlemma p_eq : p = g + h := by\\n  simp [p, g, h]\\n  ring\\n\\n/-- The degree of p is 10. -/\\nlemma p_natDegree : p.natDegree = 10 := by\\n  have hp : p = X ^ 10 + C (5 : ℂ) * X ^ 3 + C (2 : ℂ) * X + C (1 : ℂ) := rfl\\n  rw [hp]\\n  apply Polynomial.natDegree_add_of_degree_lt\\n  · simp [Polynomial.natDegree_C]\\n    sorry\\n  sorry\\n\\n/-- p has no roots on the unit circle |z| = 1.\\n\\n    Proof: if |z| = 1 and p(z) = 0, then |z¹⁰ + 1| = |5z³ + 2z|.\\n    But |5z³ + 2z| ≥ 5 − 2 = 3 and |z¹⁰ + 1| ≤ 2. Contradiction. -/\\nlemma p_no_roots_on_cir